# Line endings — the repository stores LF.
#
# Windows checkouts carry CRLF (core.autocrlf=true), and git must normalise
# that back to LF on stage or every edit shows up as a whole-file diff. The
# `text` attribute is FORCED (not `text=auto`) on purpose: auto-detection once
# mis-flagged the locale dictionaries as binary — a stray `CR CR LF` run in
# `src/client/locales-*.ts` tripped the heuristic — and `-text` files skip
# normalisation entirely, so a 4-line translation edit landed as 403/403.
# Forcing the attribute makes the guess irrelevant.
* text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalise.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
